    "articles": [
      {
        "sequence_id": 1,
        "text": "In a social situation such as this it would be natural for the German to use Mr. Allen's title in speaking to him, just as he would say \"gnädige Frau\" in speaking to a lady. An American of course would just say \"Mr. Allen\" or \"Mrs. Jones\".\nIn the German educational system after Elementary School (die Volksschule) there are two principal secondary schools for students planning to go on to the university. One is the Oberrealschule, or the Realgymnasium where modern languages and natural sciences are given prominence. The other is the Humanistisches Gymnasium, often referred to just as Gymnasium, where the humanities, classical languages and literature are given more prominence.\nanderthalb Stunden is plural in German (it is more than one), although in English we say \"an hour and a half\" and the noun remains singular.\nsich sehen. The pronoun here indicates a reciprocal relationship: \"see each other, see one another\". The pronouns sich, uns, euch may occur with a number of German verbs to indicate this relationship: besuchen, kennen, schreiben, treffen, verstehen, etc."
      }
